			[ 'How do I get rid of dust mites in my bed?', 'Wash bedding weekly at 60°C if the fabric allows, use allergen-proof covers on the mattress and pillows, and vacuum the mattress regularly. Keeping the bedroom well ventilated and less humid also helps.' ],
			[ 'Is it better to dust with a wet or dry cloth for allergies?', 'A slightly damp microfibre cloth is better. It traps dust instead of throwing it into the air, where it can be breathed in.' ],
			[ 'Does vacuuming make allergies worse?', 'It can briefly stir up dust, especially with a vacuum that leaks fine particles. A sealed vacuum with a HEPA filter, emptied outdoors, keeps allergens contained.' ],
